./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/post_role_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:2956:    "rationale": "The current crop is too broad because it includes the full pretraining architecture, while the route evidence is specifically the LLM-enriched text curation interface in Figure 1A. A tighter crop within the same figure is defensible: it visibly shows the route-specific text object (“Chunk”/cell description text), the retrieval mechanism (Retriever, Database), and the immediate LLM input path formed from standardized text plus retrieved snippets. Under the atlas rules, the exact variant name and a mandatory model-input textbox are not required when the depicted input mechanism is clear, and pretraining-time inputs are in scope.",
