./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/post_role_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:9021:          "Figure 1 overview does not visibly show gene/chromosome context text, a paired DNA-plus-context prompt, or a labeled text-embedding/fusion interface.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/post_role_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:9115:      "caption": "Figure 1: Training dynamics define distinct generalization regimes in biological reasoning models. We compare backbone choice, continued pre-training (CPT), supervised fine-tuning (SFT), and reinforcement learning (RL) across genomics, transcriptomics, and protein tasks, and evaluate each stage on biologically meaningful in-domain (ID) and out-of-domain (OOD) splits.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/post_role_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:9131:    "rationale": "The current crop is too narrow because it isolates only the Proteins task panel and drops the adjacent backbone context. A better crop exists in the same figure: include the full left-to-center overview through the Biological Modalities section so the reader can see both the protein sequence representation and the paper’s protein foundation model reference (ESM3). Under the atlas rules, a shared architecture/overview figure can support a route when it visibly depicts the route-specific input object or representation, and a model box is not mandatory. This is defensible for the ESM-3 protein embedding route at a high level, but not for the protein metadata prompt, because the figure does not show the structured text prompt blocks or prompt-token interface.",
