./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7389:        "caption": "Figure 1: Landscape of TeamPath (a) Steps of dataset curation. We extract image-text pairs from a processed TCGA dataset (PathGen-1.6M). (b) Word cloud visualization of ROI captions (upper) and questions (bottom). (c) The core visual language model architecture of TeamPath. (d) TeamPath as a system with an LLM-enhanced router (with over 80% accuracy in choosing the correct approach) and the corresponding capacities in various downstream applications. The logo fire means that we need to adjust the parameters of models, and the logo snowflake means that we do not change the parameters. (e) Overall ranking list of different methods across tasks and metrics. A lower rank (larger bubble) means a better method.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7630:        "caption": "Figure 1: Overview of RVQ-Alpha. Top: An RVQ Encoder discretizes gene expressions, followed by a progressive Pretrain-SFT-RL alignment with an LLM to enable multi-modal reasoning. Bottom: The unified model drives diverse downstream applications, spanning single-cell, population, and perturbation analyses.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7710:        "caption": "Figure 10: Semantic confusion matrix for homogeneous cell-type classification. 18 × 18 Coarse Ontology heatmap on the held-out evaluation set. The diagonal dominates (8,795 Enterocyte cells are correctly classified), and most off-diagonal mass concentrates between ontologically adjacent cell types (1,876 Enteroendocrine and Tuft cells are predicted as Goblet), demonstrating that RVQ tokenization preserves local semantic structure of gene expression.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7718:        "caption": "Figure 11: RVQ embedding space by cell type. t-SNE visualization with perplexity 50 of LLM input embeddings for RVQ-encoded cells. For each cell, the 8 codebook embeddings from the model's expanded vocabulary are averaged to produce a single cell-level representation (26 cell types, N = 1,601 cells). Biologically related cell types cluster together: Neuron ( n = 366, upper right) forms a distinct cluster; immune subtypes (CD4+ T, n = 204; Myeloid, n = 201; T/NK, n = 117; CD8+ T, n = 83) overlap at center-left; epithelial types (Enterocyte, n = 58; Goblet, n = 18) form compact clusters. The separation of neuronal from immune and epithelial lineages demonstrates that RVQ tokenization preserves major biological axes in the LLM embedding space, complementing the classification-level evidence in Figure 10.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7734:        "caption": "Figure 13: Semantic confusion matrix for homogeneous tissue-type classification. Companion to the cell-type confusion matrix in Figure 10. A 10 × 10 heatmap covering Ileum, Colon, PBMC, Entorhinal Cortex, Adrenal Gland, Lymph Node, Chest Wall, Neck, Liver, and Nose (the converged GSPO tissue policy; best-of-32 sampling; offline evaluation judge threshold 0.75, the tissue-population operating point of §4.5; external test sets D101, D102, and D103, defined in §4.5). Overall diagonal mass 13,833/16,651 ≈ 83.1%. Ileum dominates the diagonal (7,156, matrix maximum), followed by Colon (5,014). The largest off-diagonal cell is Colon → Ileum (1,294), with a smaller reciprocal Ileum → Colon (519), reflecting mutual confusion between gut tissues. Chest Wall, Neck, and Liver have diagonal zeros-Liver acts as a catch-all incorrect prediction for several rare tissues (receiving Ileum → Liver 361, Colon → Liver 242, PBMC → Liver ∼ 200), absorbing mass it never correctly predicts itself. The gut-tissue dominance and Liver sink pattern are consistent with the training data's tissue frequency distribution.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7750:        "caption": "Figure 15: Per-cell-type accuracy distribution - cell type classification. Lollipop chart of percell-type accuracy on the homogeneous cell-type task (the converged GSPO cell-type policy; offline evaluation judge threshold 0.75; 9 lineage groups). High tier ( ≥ 0.8): B cell, Plasma cell, and Enterocyte BEST4+ all achieve 1.000, along with Stem cell OLFM4+ (0.991), Excitatory neuron (0.953), Enterocyte CA1+CA2+CA4 -(0.900), Paneth cell (0.856), and Goblet cell SPINK4+ (0.830). Medium tier : Microglia (0.777), Stem cell OLFM4+ LGR5+ (0.724), Goblet cell MUC2+ TFF1 -(0.700), Inhibitory neuron (0.660), Goblet cell MUC2+ TFF1+ (0.655). Low tier : Dendritic cell (0.020), Enteroendocrine cell (0.020), and three zero-accuracy types (Multiplet, Red blood cell, Tuft cell). The long lower tail reflects rare and ontologically proximate cell types that the model struggles to distinguish.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7758:        "caption": "Figure 16: Per-cell-type accuracy distribution - tissue type classification. Lollipop chart of percell-type accuracy on the homogeneous tissue-type task (the converged GSPO tissue policy; offline evaluation judge threshold 0.75; 10 lineage groups including separate NK/ILC and Stromal lineages). High tier : only two cell types qualify-Enterocyte TMIGD1+ MEP1A+ (0.901) and Stem cell OLFM4+ GSTA1+ (0.811)-far fewer than the eight High-tier entries in Figure 15. Medium tier : Secretory cell (0.719), Excitatory neuron (0.697), Oligodendrocyte precursor (0.691), Epithelial cell METTL12+ (0.603), Innate lymphoid cell (0.508), CD8+ T cell (0.422), CD4+ T cell FOSB+ (0.406), CD8+ T cell KLRG1+ (0.405). Low tier : includes Macrophage Metallothionein+ (0.245), Fibroblast SFRP2+ SLPI+ (0.115), and three zero-accuracy types (Adrenal cortical cell, Schwann cell, Fibroblast). The contraction of the High tier from eight to two entries foreshadows the cross-task difficulty gradient.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7766:        "caption": "Figure 17: Per-cell-type accuracy distribution - disease state classification. Lollipop chart of percell-type accuracy on the homogeneous disease-state task (the converged GSPO disease-state policy; offline evaluation judge threshold 0.85-stricter than the 0.75 used for cell and tissue type, reflecting more demanding evaluation for disease state). No cell type reaches the High tier ( ≥ 0.8), completing the difficulty gradient cell type (8 High) → tissue type (2 High) → disease state (0 High). Medium tier : only Inhibitory neuron (0.519) and Excitatory neuron (0.424). Low tier : Oligodendrocyte precursor (0.385), Pericyte RERGL+ NTRK2+ (0.292), Astrocyte (0.248), Fibroblast SFRP2+ SLPI+ (0.167), Stem cell OLFM4+ LGR5+ (0.101), Glial cell (0.051), Endothelial cell DARC+ (0.020), Platelet (0.006), plus eight zero-accuracy types (NK-like cell, B cell, Macrophage Metallothionein+, Monocyte CHI3L1+, Intraepithelial lymphocyte, CD8+ T cell KLRG1+, Regulatory T cell, and T cell). The absence of any High-tier entry and the prevalence of zero-accuracy immune cell types confirm that disease-state prediction is the hardest of the three homogeneous-population tasks.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7774:        "caption": "Figure 18: Tissue type - response length vs. accuracy. Companion to Figure 9a for homogeneous tissue-type classification (the converged GSPO tissue policy). Three training phases are annotated: Initial ( ∼ 0-150 steps), Converging ( ∼ 150-300), and Stable ( ∼ 300-770). Response length (teal, rolling window of 25 steps) starts ∼ 1,500 tokens, peaks at ∼ 7,700 around steps 180-200, and settles to ∼ 6,0006,200 in the Stable phase. LLM judge accuracy (coral, rolling window of 5 steps) starts ∼ 0.44, climbs to ∼ 0.62 near step 190, then hovers at 0.55-0.61 through the Stable phase with local peaks ∼ 0.61 near steps 430-440 and 570-620. Both curves exhibit a much smaller dynamic range than the cell-type figure (Figure 9a), suggesting that the tissue-type task reaches a training plateau earlier and with less dramatic length compression.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:7782:        "caption": "Figure 19: Disease state - response length vs. accuracy. Companion to Figure 9a for homogeneous disease-state classification (the converged GSPO disease-state policy). Three phases: Initial ( ∼ 0-120 steps), Converging ( ∼ 120-260), Stable ( ∼ 260-610). Response length (teal) starts ∼ 1,500-1,600 tokens, peaks at ∼ 7,800-7,900 around step 290, then fluctuates between 6,500-7,100 through the Stable phase. Accuracy (coral) occupies the narrowest range of the three tasks (0.28-0.42): it starts ∼ 0.30, rises to ∼ 0.35 by step 40, drops to a trough of ∼ 0.285-0.29 around step 240 in the Converging phase, then rebounds unevenly through Stable with oscillations ( ∼ 0.39-0.40 at step 420, dip to ∼ 0.36 at step 480, peak ∼ 0.41 at step 535), ending near ∼ 0.40. Disease state shows the weakest length-compression effect and the noisiest accuracy trajectory, consistent with it being the hardest task.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/adjudication_manifest.json:8127:        "caption": "Figure 1: Token analysis, BFT, and applications. a : Semantic composition of low-confidence tokens inside Group A (sparse-low) and Group B (dense-low). b : 4096-token trace illustrating one sparse-low window (Group A) and one dense-low window (Group B). c : BFT applies token- and sample-level loss adjustments. d : BFT-generated biomedical profiles are encoded by a text embedding model for downstream representation tasks.",
