./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/final_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:2311:    "rationale": "Figure 1 directly depicts the listed model-input pathway: single-cell RNA-seq profiles pass through the cell encoder to gene embeddings, then a modality adapter/projected embedding stage, and these are concatenated with instruction and prompt embeddings at the decoder interface. Under the atlas rules, the exact variant name need not appear when the same paper’s shared architecture shows the same input mechanism for the named variant. The crop is input-focused and valid for both the gene-expression conditioning route and the prompt-conditioning route.",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/final_crossvalidated_crop_ledger.json:2392:        "rationale": "Figure 1 directly depicts the actual model-input pathway for this paper: single-cell RNA-seq profiles are transformed through the cell encoder and adapter into projected gene embeddings, which are concatenated with instruction and prompt embeddings and fed to the language model decoder. Under the atlas rules, a shared architecture figure can support named variants from the same paper when the depicted input mechanism is the same, so the absence of a visible 'Llama-1B' label does not invalidate the crop. The current crop already includes the relevant input object, representation, transformation, and immediate decoder interface for both supported routes.",
