ot mutations, Question = Which cell lines have a mutation in the gene EP300?. Hotspot mutations, Answer = 639V, CAL33, HEC1A, HEC265, JHH5, NCIH1618, NO11, RL, SKOV3, SNU81, SUDHL10, TE12. Mutated oncogenes, Question = Which oncogenes are mutated in cell line SF126<omics>, sorted alphabetically?. Mutated oncogenes, Answer = TERT. Mutated TSGs, Question = Which tumor suppressor genes (tsg) are mutated in cell line SNU1077<omics>, sorted alphabetically?. Mutated TSGs, Answer = TP53. Cell line disease, Question = Which disease context is associated with the origin of the LAN6 cell line?. Cell line disease, Answer = The donor of LAN6 has neuroblastoma.. Cell line lineage, Question = What type of lineage characterizes the NCIBL2009 cell line?. Cell line lineage, Answer = NCIBL2009 is of lineage lymphoid.. Cell line mutations, Question = What genetic mutation is present in the HSPSS<omics> cell line?. Cell line mutations, Answer = The gene deletion of gene(s) CDKN2B is a genetic characteristic of HSPSS.. Cell line primary site, Question = What is the tissue of origin for the NB1643<omics> cell line?. Cell line primary site, Answer = Abdomen is the origin of the NB1643.. Transformant type, Question = What was used to transform the PRECLH<omics> cell line?. Transformant type, Answer = The Simian virus 40 (SV40) transformed PRECLH.. Cell line description, Question = What are some basic information about cell line NCIBL2087?. Cell line description, Answer = NCIBL2087 is an Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) transformed, non-cancerous lymphoid cell line derived from a 69-year- old adult caucasian male that grows in. Most similar cell line, Question = Given cell lines LN18<omics>, HKA1<omics>, SBC5<omics>, LS513<omics>, KYSE270<omics>, which of them is the most similar to HARA<omics> in terms of expression profile?. Most similar cell line, Answer = KYSE270.\n\nMost similar pair, Question = Given cell lines DND41<omics>, CFPAC1<omics>, A375SKINCJ1<omics>, TALL1<omics>, SNU182<omics>, NCIH524<omics>, which pair is the most similar in terms of expression profile?. Most\n\nA Appendix\nA.7 Task Examples\n similar pair, Answer = TALL1, DND41\n(continued on next page)\n\n\nA Appendix A.7 Task Examples (continued from previous page) Pathways, Question = . Pathways, Answer = . Path reachability, Question = Is LRP1 accessible from REG4 in the pathways, not necessar- ily directly?. Path reachability, Answer = No. Edge existence, Question = Is there an 'indirect effect' direct relationship from PRKAG2 to SREBF1?. Edge existence, Answer = Yes. Random walk, Question = Show me a sequence of connections starting from FST in the network.. Random walk, Answer = FST inhibit INHBA activate ACVR1C activate SMAD3 express RORC express IL17F. Knockout path completion, Question = If the following nodes are knocked out: [PRKACA, JUN, SRC, PRKCA, PRKCB], what is the shortest path from IpaB to CSF3 in the biological pathways?. Knockout path completion, Answer = IpaB activate ITGB1 bind to PRKCG activate FOS express CSF3. Path completion, Question = Complete the following biological pathway in the downstream direction: GNB5. Path completion, Answer = activate MAPK14 activate FOSB expres- sion DEFB4A. Name → network elements, Question = In the context of 'Long patch BER', complete the following biological pathway in the downstream direction: POLB. Name → network elements, Answer = form complex with MCM7 form complex with PCNA form complex with RFC2 activate FEN1 activate LIG1. Name → pathways, Question = In the context of 'Epstein-Barr virus infection', complete the following biological pathway in the downstream direction: SKP2. Name → pathways, Answer = activate RB1 unknown relationship E2F1. Elements → geneset name, Question = Given the following biological pathway sequence in the downstream direction: NKX3-1 unknown relationship AKT1 inhibit BAD, which pathway or geneset does this represent?. Elements → geneset name, Answer = Loss of NKX3-1 to PI3K signaling pathway. Pathways → geneset name, Question = Given the following biological pathway sequence in the downstream direction: CALM3 activate CAMK1D activate CREB3L4 cause expression CYP11B2, which pathway or geneset does this represent?. Pathways → geneset name, Answer = Aldosterone synthesis and secretion. Pathway neighbors, Question = What are the interactions with other proteins for FARSB?. Pathway neighbors, Answer = Interactions for FARSB: FARSB un- known relationship with EEF1B2, FARSB unknown relationship with EPRS1, FARSB bind with FARS2, FARSB bind with FARSA, F. . .. Genes → pathways, Question = Which pathway is related to the following gene set: TRAF6, MAP3K7, TAB2?. Genes → pathways, Answer = HSV US3 to TLR2/4-NFKB signaling pathway. Pathways → genes, Question = Which genes are related to HSV US3 to TLR2/4-NFKB signaling pathway?. Pathways → genes, Answer = TRAF6, MAP3K7, TAB2. Pathway enrichment, Question = Given the top overexpressed genes in cell line MESSA<omics>, what are the top 20 upregulated pathways?. Pathway enrichment, Answer = The following pathways are upregulated: Metals to KEAP1-NRF2 signalig pathway, Regulation of fibrinolytic system, C1INH, Yersinia YopP/J to TLR2/4-MAP....\n\nGene set composition, Question = Which biological process is related to the following gene\n\nA Appendix\nA.7 Task Examples\n set: GSN, TGFB1, BIK, SH3GLB1, ISL1, MAPK15, SELENOP, PINK1, IAPP, UBLCP1, TRABD2A, BAX, PREB, ULK1, AJUBA, STX1B, TRABD2B, NAPB, RB1, STXBP1, RALB, HJURP, CLU, PARK7, TNF, TANK, BCL2L11, CDH5, NCLN, HSF1, LAMP2, VPS1.... Gene set composition, Answer = Regulation of Protein-Containing Com- plex Assembly. Gene set enrichment, Question = Which biological processes are related to the following gene set: ATF4, HTRA2, PPIA, INS, BAG5?. Gene set enrichment, Answer = Negative Regulation of Oxidative Stress- Induced Intrinsic Apoptotic Signaling Pathway, Regulation of Oxidative Stress- Induced Intrinsic Apoptotic Sign. . .. LCA completion, Question = In biological pathways, what is the shortest common upstream node (Lowest Common Ancestor, LCA) for ELK1 and NCAM2? Describe the respective upstream paths from ELK1 to this LCA and from NCAM2 to this LCA.. LCA completion, Answer = The upstream path from ELK1 to the LCA is PRNP inhibit HSPA5 inhibit ERN1 activate MAPK8 activate ELK1. The upstream path from NCAM2 to the LCA is PRN.... Protein, Question = . Protein, Answer = . Protein properties, Question = What are the type properties of protein MAP2K6?. Protein properties, Answer = MAP2K6 (Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase 6 ia a enzyme and kinase protein.. Protein functions, Question = What can be a function of the protein MYOD1?. Protein functions, Answer = Acts as a transcriptional activator that promotes transcription of muscle-specific target genes and plays a role in muscle differentiation. Subcellular location, Question = What are possible locations of protein RFPL4A?. Subcellular location, Answer = Protein RFPL4A could be located in: centrosome, cytosol.\n\nA Appendix\nA.8 Asset Provenance, Licenses, and Terms of Use\nThis section consolidates the third-party assets used for training, evaluation, and implementation in this work. For each asset we report the version (where applicable), the original creator or maintainer, a citation and URL, the license, and how we use it. Asset usage was verified against each license at the time of submission.\nNon-commercial restrictions. X-Atlas/Orion is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; commercial use and redistribution under different terms are not permitted. It is used exclusively for noncommercial research in this work.\nGTEx acknowledgement. The GTEx data used in this work were obtained from GTEx Analysis Release V10 (dbGaP Accession phs000424.v10.p2).\nDepMapcompliance note. DepMap 24Q4 data are used to fine-tune OmicsLM for gene-essentiality and cell-line genomics tasks. The Broad Institute DepMap Terms of Use permit training AI/ML models on the data for internal research use, including non-profit sharing of methodologies . This work is conducted exclusively as non-commercial academic research. The raw DepMap files are not redistributed in our released artifacts.\n\n\nA Appendix A.8 Asset Provenance, Licenses, and Terms of Use Table 10: Third-party assets used in OmicsLM and in evaluation. Expression datasets, Version = Expression datasets. Expression datasets, Owner / Main- tainer = Expression datasets. Expression datasets, Citation&URL = Expression datasets. Expression datasets, License / Terms = Expression datasets. Expression datasets, Use in this work = Expression datasets. Human Cell Atlas, Version = CellxGene Census 2025- 01-30. Human Cell Atlas, Owner / Main- tainer = Chan Zuckerberg Initiative. Human Cell Atlas, Citation&URL = [Regev et al., 2017, Chan Zuckerberg Ini- tiative, 2025]; https: //cellxgene. cziscience.com/. Human Cell Atlas, License / Terms = CC BY 4.0. Human Cell Atlas, Use in this work = Primary training source for single-cell annotation tasks.. Tabula Sapiens, Version = GEO: GSE201048. Tabula Sapiens, Owner / Main- tainer = The Tabula Sapi- ens Consortium. Tabula Sapiens, Citation&URL = [The Tabula Sapiens Consortium, 2022]; https://www.ncbi. nlm.nih.gov/geo/ query/acc.cgi? acc=GSE201048. Tabula Sapiens, License / Terms = CC BY 4.0. Tabula Sapiens, Use in this work = Held-out evaluation benchmark (cell-type annotation); not used in training.. GTEx, Version = v10; dbGaP phs000424.v10.p2. GTEx, Owner / Main- tainer = NIH Common Fund. GTEx, Citation&URL = [GTEx Consortium, 2020]; https:// gtexportal.org/. GTEx, License / Terms = GTEx Portal terms of use. GTEx, Use in this work = Tissue-of-origin predic- tion (training + evalua- tion). Acknowledgement phrase in Acknowledge- ments section.. TCGA, Version = GDC Open Access. TCGA, Owner / Main- tainer = NCI / NHGRI. TCGA, Citation&URL = [Weinstein et al., 2013]; https: //portal.gdc. cancer.gov/. TCGA, License / Terms = NIH Genomic Data Sharing Policy. TCGA, Use in this work 